WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.735
A useful message connects a benefit with a clear next
step.

2
00:00:03.935 --> 00:00:08.059
Our fictional announcement says: Need a predictable
quiet place to study?

3
00:00:08.259 --> 00:00:10.845
Check the quiet-use periods on the room schedule.

4
00:00:11.045 --> 00:00:15.555
That message is appropriate only if the schedule and
service support the promise.

5
00:00:15.755 --> 00:00:21.511
Public relations develops an ongoing relationship and
mutual understanding with the community.

6
00:00:21.711 --> 00:00:25.873
Publicity creates awareness, for example through a
community news story.

7
00:00:26.073 --> 00:00:29.005
Advertising involves paid promotional placement.

8
00:00:29.205 --> 00:00:32.544
They can support marketing, but none is the whole
process.

9
00:00:32.744 --> 00:00:38.631
Choose channels that intended users actually encounter,
including options beyond social media.

10
00:00:38.831 --> 00:00:41.554
Prepare staff to answer questions consistently.

11
00:00:41.754 --> 00:00:42.994
Then evaluate.

12
00:00:43.194 --> 00:00:48.532
Reach tells us who may have seen a message; room use
tells us something about participation.

13
00:00:48.732 --> 00:00:51.987
Neither alone shows that people found suitable space.

14
00:00:52.187 --> 00:00:57.245
Compare feedback, unmet requests, access barriers, and
workload with the objective.

15
00:00:57.445 --> 00:01:01.008
Keep what works, adjust what does not, and explain the
change.

16
00:01:01.208 --> 00:01:03.852
That returns us to the start of the planning cycle.

